      "tips": [
        {
          "text": "Practicing from IndiaBix is more than sufficient for this round. Focus on time management and attempt easier questions first. Regular practice on compound interest, ratios, and seating arrangements is recommended.",
          "category": "OA preparation",
          "page": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Be confident and conversational. Know your resume thoroughly, especially your projects - be ready to explain what problem each project solves in simple terms. Research the company beforehand so you can speak about their work culture with some awareness.",
          "category": "HR preparation",
          "page": 2
        },
        {
          "text": "Revise OOP concepts (Encapsulation, Abstraction, Inheritance, Polymorphism) and have a concrete example from your own project ready for each. Be comfortable explaining your projects and internship work end-to-end. Practice basic system design - especially around databases, storage, and API design - as scenario-based questions are common.",
          "category": "Technical preparation",
          "page": 2
        },
        {
          "text": "Listen actively and ask thoughtful questions about the role, team structure, or learning opportunities. This is your chance to show genuine interest in the company.",
          "category": "HR preparation",
          "page": 3
        },
        {
          "text": "Even though this round feels relaxed, remain professional. Show enthusiasm about the opportunity and the company. Asking one or two genuine questions about the role or the team leaves a positive impression.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 3
        }
